      "id": "jin10:20261127003925410800",
      "title": "UNCTAD: Global maritime trade volume forecast to stagnate in 2026",
      "url": "https://www.jin10.com/#/flash/20261127003925410800",
      "source": "jin10",
      "source_name": "金十数据",
      "author": "",
      "summary": "UNCTAD said global maritime trade volume is forecast to post zero growth in 2026, down from 1.9% in 2025, as geopolitical uncertainty weighs on shipping. Pressure on the Strait of Hormuz, Red Sea, Black Sea and Panama Canal is forcing vessels onto longer, costlier routes. More than 80% of global trade by volume moves by sea, including food and fuel. Rerouting keeps goods moving but increases transit times and costs, particularly for smaller economies. If elevated marine fuel costs persist through 2027, higher shipping costs alone could push consumer prices in least-developed countries to nearly twice the global average.",
      "content": "",
      "title_zh": "",
      "summary_zh": "",
      "published_at": "2026-11-27T00:39:25+08:00",
